{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>For</b> — And the trustworthy witness to our words is that we willingly are killed for the sake of the glory of Your name, and willingly we are counted as sheep for slaughter, even though we are sons of noblemen, better than those who slaughter us. And this word is like: 'chief of the slaughterers' (רב הטבחים)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {0 "The phrase בני איש (literally 'sons of a man') is read here as 'sons of a nobleman'; the cross-reference רב הטבחים alludes to Genesis 37:36."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:48.298620255Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}